  "year": 2005,
  "summary": "MF82 frame card: one 75 Ω AES/EBU input, cable EQ, a CS8427 receiver that re-times it to four 75 Ω outputs, and a DAC feeding two balanced analog stereo pairs. The archived PIC firmware (v100, 2005|38) is for the ISS1 board with a DIP switch for reference level and routing; the shipping ISS3 board used a PIC16C54 whose code is lost.",
  "highlights": [
   "Board from the real ISS3 assembly drawing; ISS1 drawn from its pick-and-place file",
   "DIP switch → computed-GOTO tables → CS4392 registers, bit by bit",
   "Main loop timed from the code: 6303 cycles = 5.13 ms",
   "Glitch → latched UNLOCK → TXOFF one pass later",
   "Cable length and EQ modelled from the part values",
   "Firmware drives a second receiver that is not on the board"
  ],
