  "year": 1997,
  "summary": "Half-rack AES/EBU monitor: a CS8412 receiver feeds a CS4330 DAC for balanced, unbalanced and headset outputs, analog VU detectors drive two 20-LED bars, and a PIC16C73A turns the receiver's error and rate codes into eight status lamps while multiplexing the bars. Modelled from the archived V1.00/V1.01/V10X assembly source and the ISS3 netlist.",
  "highlights": [
   "Real silkscreen separations from POD11SLK.CDR with live bars and lamps",
   "Pass-by-pass model of the PIC firmware: CBL sync, TABLE1/TABLE2, L/R multiplex",
   "Power-up lamp chase and the watchdog-only recovery from loss of lock",
   "VU ballistics computed from the Rauch filter values (2.3 Hz, Q 0.56)",
   "Finds the swapped lamp-test labels and the CONSUMER/PRO inversion",
   "Answers where POD11A's firmware is (SLM-1D, not POD3A)"
  ],
